    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **278 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city title-casing / reuse rule for owner creation in `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`:\n\nIn `saveOwner`, for new owners only, the city is now resolved via a new `resolveCity(owner)` call before the customer code is generated:\n\n- **`resolveCity`** \u2014 scans existing owners for one whose city matches (case-insensitively). If found, it returns that owner's *exact* spelling so the whole clinic agrees on one canonical form; otherwise it falls back to title-casing the supplied city.\n- **`toTitleCase`** \u2014 upper-cases the first letter of each whitespace-separated word and lower-cases the rest, preserving original whitespace (`null` stays `null`).\n\nThis slots into the existing new-owner block alongside registration date, membership number, customer code, and duplicate checks. It's confined to the create path (`owner.isNew()`), so updates are untouched, and it plays well with `generateCustomerCode` (which upper-cases the city regardless).\n\n**Tests**: The repository already contained `Cp12Tests` covering exactly this behavior (`coreTitleCasesCity` and `functionalityReusesExistingCitySpelling`) \u2014 both now pass, along with the full suite (278 tests).",
